 "lines": {
  "Daylight is best: near a window, out of direct sun.": "d6c012a48669",
  "A lamp or spotlight overhead makes glare on glossy prints, so turn it off.": "07a70073c93d",
  "Watch for the shadow of your phone and hands.": "ebaeaa5d9eb1",
  "Hold the phone flat above the print. StoryPrints straightens photos taken at an angle, but flat is best.": "c84eb422b4fe",
  "A backing that contrasts with the photo helps StoryPrints find the edges more easily:": "e28ae55efdf2",
  "dark for light photos, light for dark ones. It isn’t essential.": "2a8405cc6c6c",
  "Leave a border of backing showing all round the print, so none of its edges is cut off.": "4333d73f6830",
  "Tap Take photos.": "b4af8d47c02e",
  "Check that Prints is selected at the top, then tap the round button for each print.": "e5b5383791ff",
  "The last photo and the count show at the bottom, so you can keep going without stopping.": "74f97d366fda",
  "When you’ve finished, tap Done.": "136d5e98fc9d"
 }
}
